messages:
Alex: Quick sync request 1: were building a "1k token" unit-econ dashboard in Console. Need runtime/infra to emit signals so we can break down cost per 1k tokens + cache/batch savings. Minimal event dims: model_id, input_tokens, output_tokens, batch_size, kv_cache_hit, gpu_ms, and routing_tier. Who can own the telemetry contract?

Maria: @Alex I own the Console visuals. We need per-route and per-model dimensions so the dashboard can filter by product route. Please include route_id or route_path and model_id. Per-request aggregates (input/output token counts) are sufficient; avoid per-token events unless unavoidable.

Dmitri: eng-runtime here. We can emit model_id, input_tokens, output_tokens, batch_size, kv_cache_hit, kv_prefix_len, kernel_variant, and gpu_ms. Clarify: do you want gpu_ms as raw or normalized (gpu_ms_per_token)? We can add tokens_per_second or both.

Alex: Add tokens_per_second too. Dashboard will compute cost_per_1k = (token_cost_estimate_usd / (input_tokens+output_tokens)) * 1000 once we have token_cost_estimate_usd. Also need quantization_flag and deployment_type (hosted|dedicated|private).

Jonah: From routing/cost attribution: we need multitenant_routing_path + route_owner so we can map costs to teams. Also add fallback_to_smaller_model (bool) and fallback_reason strings so we can attribute fallbacks that change unit cost.

Sophia: Runtime already emits exec spans with gpu_ms + model_name but we don't have kv cache details. Adding kv_cache_hit and kv_prefix_len increases event size. Proposal: emit full kv metadata sampled at 1% and emit boolean kv_cache_hit and kv_prefix_len always. Include sample_rate and sample_key for any sampled blobs.

Alex: Sampling is acceptable if events include sample_rate so Console can scale sampled metrics. We need sample_key for grouping sampled rows back to a request when debugging.

Dmitri: We'll add sample_rate (double) + sample_key (string) + sampled_kv_tokens (int) in the meta. Well emit aggregated counts per request, not per-token. For heavy routes we can bump sampling for a short window.

Carla: Product ask: dashboard should show two headline tiles: "Estimated cost per 1k tokens" and "Estimated savings from cache & batching" with 95% CI. Also a small table breaking down savings by model_variant and route. Do we compute token_cost_estimate_usd in runtime or compute in the dashboard?

Maria: Prefer runtime to compute token_cost_estimate_usd using platform price_map + quant multipliers so the same value lands everywhere. The runtime sidecar can compute this asynchronously and attach estimate to the telemetry event to avoid blocking LLM latency. Include price_map_version in the event.

Jonah: Price_map varies by offer and by region. runtime needs to tag deployment_type and pricing_tier; platform should prod a canonical price_map service. Sidecar compute sounds fine. Ensure price_map_version and region are present so Console can recompute if needed.

Dmitri: Implementation plan: add an async price-sidecar that listens to events, enriches with price_map_version, computes token_cost_estimate_usd, then emits TokenEconEvent via existing telemetry pipeline. We'll include deployment_type, pricing_tier, price_map_version, and model_variant.

Sophia: Draft proto to put in specs repo (feedback welcome):
```
message TokenEconEvent {
  string model_id = 1; // e.g., redwood/gptx-16k
  string route_id = 2; // customer-visible route
  int64 input_tokens = 3;
  int64 output_tokens = 4;
  int32 batch_size = 5;
  bool kv_cache_hit = 6;
  int32 kv_prefix_len = 7; // tokens from cache
  int32 cache_prefix_hits = 8; // count of prefix hits
  double gpu_ms = 9;
  double tokens_per_second = 10;
  bool quantized = 11;
  string model_variant = 12;
  string deployment_type = 13; // hosted|dedicated|private
  double token_cost_estimate_usd = 14;
  string price_map_version = 15;
  double sample_rate = 16;
  string sample_key = 17;
  bool fallback_to_smaller_model = 18;
  string fallback_reason = 19;
}
```

Alex: This looks good. A few notes: 1) include route_owner tag for billing mapping; 2) add kernel_variant if possible for perf debugging; 3) ensure sampling defaults are decided by infra (1% for full kv payloads).

Dmitri: Will add kernel_variant and route_owner. Well default sampled_kv_payload_rate to 0.01 but make it configurable per-route. Proto PR + spec doc coming later today.

Maria: For Console mockups: we'll build tiles that compute per-1k cost and a stacked bar for savings: batch savings vs kv cache savings vs quantization. For CIs use bootstrap from sampled events; include a note about sampling adjustments. We'll need backend join keys: sample_key, route_id, model_variant.

Jonah: Platform notes: we must map multitenant_routing_path to billing buckets. I'll produce mapping table and send to eng-platform so Console can align. Also recommend a nightly rollup job to compute stable estimates for dashboards (reduce noise).

Alex: TL;DR / action items: Dmitri + Sophia push proto PR and sidecar plan; Maria + Carla build dashboard mocks and CI approach; Jonah produce route->billing mapping; Platform infra to set sampling defaults (1% kv fields); Sync Thursday 10:00am to approve telemetry contract.

deploy-bot: deploy-bot pushed branch telemetry/token-econ with commit abc123def - CI started.
